<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Deliberately free of the API 31 attributes (targetCellWidth/Height,
     description, previewLayout). minSdk is 29, so lint reports each of them as
     UnusedAttribute — and warningsAsErrors is on, so that is a failed build
     rather than a note. minWidth/minHeight size the widget on every level this
     app supports; adding the newer attributes means a res/xml-v31 variant to
     keep in step, which is a trade worth making only once they buy something.

     updatePeriodMillis is load-bearing, not a default. A day rollover is not an
     event, so nothing commits at the cutoff and ProjectionListener cannot fire
     for one — this period is the only thing that shortens how long a widget
     shows yesterday's ticks. It does not *bound* it: this is a minimum interval
     between requested updates, which the framework batches and defers under
     Doze, and it will not wake the device to deliver one. 30 minutes is also the
     floor the framework clamps to, so a smaller number would be a comment
     claiming something untrue. An exact refresh at the cutoff wants a
     WorkManager worker, scheduled by the reminder step — WorkManager itself is
     already a dependency, since Glance requires it (docs/ux/widget.md §4, §5). -->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
